# Hard-call confusion

**What this is.** Pooled across every (cluster, chrom) in the
cohort, the row-normalised confusion matrix between popout's
primary-ancestry call (argmax) and each comparison tool's
primary-ancestry call. Rows are popout labels; columns are the
tool's labels.

**How to read this chart.** Diagonal cells are agreement; the
title strip carries the overall diagonal fraction. Off-diagonal
mass on a specific row says popout systematically *re-routes*
that ancestry to a different label under that tool — for example
popout-`mid` ending up as tool-`eur` would show up as a strong
`mid -> eur` cell. Faithful rendering: no label folding in this
report — what you see is what the collector wrote.

